<?xml version="1.0" ?>
<Simulation verbosity="debug">
  <TestInfo>
    <name>framework/ROM/TimeSeries/DMD/PooledDMDC</name>
    <author>alfoa</author>
    <created>2026-10-30</created>
    <classesTested>SupervisedLearning.DMDC</classesTested>
    <description>
      This test checks the pooled identification of the DMDC ROM (pooled = True, historyOffsets = True):
      a single model (A, B and C matrices) is identified from 4 histories of the same linear system
      x[k+1] = A x[k] + B u[k] + c_s, y = C x (time constants 15 s and 300 s, see
      DMDC/trainingData/generatePooledDMDC.py), with a different constant term c_s for each history.
      The histories have different lengths: they are provided on a common time grid, extended with their last
      values, and their end time is given by the tEnd variable (validUntil).
      The exported time constants must be 15 and 300 s and the constant terms the ones used to generate
      the data. The ROM is then evaluated on the longest history (actuator level 1.6, closest training
      history in the parameter space) and must reproduce it.
    </description>
  </TestInfo>

  <RunInfo>
    <WorkingDir>DMDC/PooledDMDC</WorkingDir>
    <Sequence>readTrainData,DMDCTrain,stats,writeOut,runDMDc</Sequence>
    <batchSize>1</batchSize>
  </RunInfo>

  <Files>
    <Input name="TrainDataFile">../trainingData/Pooled_DMDC.csv</Input>
  </Files>

  <Models>
    <ROM name="DMDrom" subType="DMDC">
